# Mobile sync & verification

Authoritative standard: `.ai/MASTER_WORKFLOW.md` (§4, §12, §16).

- After regenerating `HANDOFF.md` / `CHANGELOG_SESSION.md`, run the local sync script when
  this Mac worktree is available: `~/.local/bin/sync-alphatrade-ai-handoff.sh`.
- The local sync copies ONLY those two files to the AI-Projects iCloud destination. It must
  never copy the repository, `.git`, dependencies, virtualenvs, caches, datasets, model
  artifacts, logs, secrets, or build output, and must not delete unrelated iCloud content.
- The script must: use absolute quoted paths and strict shell mode; compare content and skip
  identical files without rewriting mtimes; copy atomically (temp + rename); preserve source
  mtime; set readable permissions; verify the destination with ordinary SHA256 **and**
  `cmp`/`diff`; log concisely without secrets; return nonzero on failure; be idempotent.
- Verify actual syncs: source/destination SHA256, `cmp`/`diff`, expected destination and exit 0.
  Record verification failure as a mobile publication blocker; it does not prevent independent
  implementation or already authorized Git operations.
- Record blockers promptly and sync available checkpoints at meaningful boundaries. Absent
  Mac/iCloud/script access in cloud is an explicit unexecuted check, not a code prerequisite.
- The local LaunchAgent uses `WatchPaths` for the two files, `RunAtLoad`, and a low-frequency
  fallback interval. Preserve the existing script/LaunchAgent when they already meet this
  standard.
- **Cloud path:** batch authorized handoff publication per `.cursor/rules/70-handoff.mdc` so
  `com.alphatrade.handoff-sync` can update
  `~/Library/Mobile Documents/com~apple~CloudDocs/AlphaTrade AI/HANDOFF.md` for iPhone.
  That agent selects by newest `Generated At UTC` and must not be weakened.
- Verify remote source equality when publishing. Do not claim the downstream iCloud copy
  matched unless observed; do not add per-edit pushes or manual user-relay requirements.
